WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.236
Welcome back to OUTFRONT, where we are

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.537
following the breaking news.

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.139
The judge in Fulton County

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.273
rejecting Mark Meadows

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.542
bid to move his case to federal court

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.844
ruling that Meadows actions

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:11.911
to help Trump overturn

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.213
the election were not connected

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:14.280
to his official duties

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.949
as White House chief of staff.

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:17.250
And many legal experts

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.251
say that if Meadows

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:19.185
failed to move his case

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.587
out of Fulton County,

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:21.221
it's bad news

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:23.056
for his other 18 co-defendants,

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:24.491
including Donald Trump.

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:26.359
OUTFRONT now, the Fulton County Sheriff,

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.160
Patrick Labat.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.361
This is his first interview

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:29.195
since former President

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.063
Trump was arrested

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:32.432
and processed at the Fulton County Jail.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.200
Which sheriff Labat runs?

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.602
Jeff, I really appreciate your time.

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:36.336
Thank you so much

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:37.737
for being with me tonight.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.305
So you've got this breaking news.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:39.706
The judge

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.041
saying the trial for Mark Meadows

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:44.310
is going to stay in your county,

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:45.378
which could be a sign

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:46.713
that a lot of other cases

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:47.881
are going to stay in your county,

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.049
including that for the former

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.950
president himself.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:51.551
Bonnie Willis,

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:52.052
the D.A.,

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.720
says she wants to hold a joint trial

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.588
for all of them starting next month.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:56.823
She says it'd be for months.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:57.657
The judge said it could

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:00.026
easily be as many as eight.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:02.295
We all saw your security preparations.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:02.829
How tight

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.798
and how involved, how intensive

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:05.432
and exhausting

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.766
they were for the one day

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:07.867
Trump surrendered.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.602
How do you sustain that for

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:10.503
maybe eight months?

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:12.272
Well, first,

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.307
I'm very proud of the women and men

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:16.142
for the county sheriff's office,

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.811
as well as the many

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:18.945
local and state partners

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:21.214
that really jumped in to help.

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:23.083
It was very well thought out plan.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.117
And to your point,

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:26.519
it will be we'll create a rotation

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:27.420
to help sustain

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.355
something of that magnitude.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.424
We have here in Fulton County a little

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.159
a little expertize

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.595
in working with these situations.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.530
We've had large trials before.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.965
Nothing of this magnitude

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.200
in terms of the status,

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.367
but we certainly

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.603
will live up to the opportunity

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.538
to show how well Fulton County

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:48.274
and the sheriff's office present Right.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:48.475
Right.

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:49.809
I mean, because that would be you know,

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:50.844
that's running a marathon.

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:52.212
It's not a sprint, as you say.

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:53.446
That would be day in and day out

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.948
for months and months.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:55.281
Of course,

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:55.715
you were there,

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:56.416
Sheriff, of former

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.485
President Trump's entire booking process.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:01:59.252
You know,

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.487
you and I had spoken before

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:01.821
and you were adamant

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:02.622
that Trump would be treated

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:03.690
like any other defendant.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.024
And you did that.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.392
That included his mug shot

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.927
as something that had not incurred in

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:08.895
his other indictments.

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:12.332
You were there with him in your jail.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.633
What was that like for you?

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.701
How would you

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.836
how could you describe his demeanor

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:19.305
as he was being booked?

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.773
Well, I will tell you, having

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:21.541
having been

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.476
in law enforcement for 32 years,

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:25.411
having been in a jail environment

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.646
equally as long.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.548
It was eerily quiet

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:29.349
when you have that

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:31.484
many security protocols in place.

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.520
I will tell you, he came out

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.054
he was very stoic,

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.023
really, really in a space

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.791
that he was able to

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.393
really lean on what we were doing,

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:41.294
what we planned.

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:42.362
And so we took his mug

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.063
shot, took his fingerprints

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.865
as we would anybody else.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.233
And ultimately

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:49.068
we arrange for his bond paperwork

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.503
to be brought to the motorcade

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.672
so that we could get him in and off

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.707
the premises as quickly as possible.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:55.175
It's interesting

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.676
when you describe his demeanor

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.511
as stoic, that it was eerily silent

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.546
when you went through all that,

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:01.548
the mug shot, the fingerprinting,

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:03.449
did he say anything?

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:03.883
Did he have any

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.585
conversation or was he silent

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:08.254
No, he was pretty silent.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.522
We spoke.

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:12.258
I came, gave very clear instructions.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.893
He took the mug shot

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.695
and like anybody else, took

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:16.462
his fingerprints

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:17.463
and again,

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:19.966
he was in and out pretty quickly

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:21.334
and had no issue with any of it.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.235
I mean, not that he could have,

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:23.803
but I mean, he was

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.405
in terms of his face, as you say,

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:26.372
it was just it was stoic.

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.107
There was no expression.

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:31.010
Now, it was, again, eerily silent.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:34.614
And really, it was for me

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:36.015
on a personal level,

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:38.451
it was heartbreaking to see

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:39.953
someone of that stature

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:41.688
and who represents our country

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:42.855
in that fashion

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:43.923
having to go through this.

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:44.924
But again,

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:45.925
women and men of the Fulton

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.694
County Sheriff's Office, both our sworn

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:48.995
and professional team,

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.797
very, very, very professional

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:53.032
and making sure that we follow through

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:54.701
not only with our commitment

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:55.768
to serve our community,

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:58.438
but really focus on the job at hand and

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.106
and get the former president out.

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:02.508
It's interesting how you describe it.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:03.142
It's heartbreaking

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:04.110
because it's, I think, important

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:04.444
for people

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:04.911
to remember

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:05.612
that it should be

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.981
for everybody, everybody in this country.

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:10.583
Trump did, of course, when he walked out,

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.585
he grabbed that mug shot and ran with it.

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:13.653
Proverbially

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.188
said he raised $7 million

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:16.756
in just a few days.

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:18.224
He put out

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:19.926
T-shirts and coffee mugs with the image.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:20.760
Right. He owned it.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:21.160
He owned it.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.162
And he used it to raise a lot of money.

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:25.598
And then he said this about it

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:29.168
I think the fake indictment

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:30.136
that they did in

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:31.804
Georgia was very helpful.

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:34.140
And then they insisted on a mug shot

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:34.707
and somehow

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:38.111
it turned out to be a very iconic

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:38.911
sheriff.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:39.746
In retrospect,

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:41.281
do you think that it was a mistake

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:41.514
at all?

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:42.282
Do you have any regrets

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:44.217
about doing the mug shot?

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:44.417
You know,

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.184
given that he, of course,

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:47.654
has capitalized off it in a massively

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:48.488
lucrative way?

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:50.657
Well, if

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:52.258
there were any regrets,

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:53.192
the copywriting,

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:54.527
I leave that up to the lawyers.

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:56.529
There is still an opportunity for us to

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:58.231
hopefully partake

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:00.199
in some of the capitalization of that

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.100
and then put it back

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.235
in the sheriff's office.

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:03.169
We don't know.

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:03.870
We'll leave that up

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.805
to the legal legal beagles,

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:07.974
if you will, to make sure that they

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:09.942
really are that keep around here as well.

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:12.245
So we are focusing on, again,

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:14.280
our making sure we maintain

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.549
as safe as possible facility

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:20.019
we can as well as again, I understand

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.555
the capitalization of it.

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:24.223
And maybe that was the plan all along.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:24.891
We don't know.

00:05:24.891 --> 00:05:25.992
But we're in a place

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:27.860
to maintain our commitment,

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.362
make sure we focus on

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:31.964
treating everybody's humanely as we can.

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:32.265
All right.

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:33.599
And to that point, Sheriff,

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:34.500
I do want to ask you about,

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.468
of course, a lot of the news

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:37.203
out there about your facility

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:37.904
when you talk about, you know,

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:39.472
treating people as safely as possible.

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:40.940
Trump has obviously attacked

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.008
your jail conditions there.

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:43.843
One of the fundraising emails,

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:44.911
he said in part,

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:46.045
while I was being arrested,

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:47.513
I got a firsthand look at the poor

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:49.182
and disgraceful conditions of the Fulton

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:50.249
County Jail.

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:51.784
It's worse than you can imagine.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:52.652
It's violent.

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:54.120
The building is falling apart.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.421
Seeing the third world state of that

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:56.856
jail, maybe even more determined

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:57.757
to run for president

00:05:57.757 --> 00:05:58.825
and save our country

00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:01.060
from permanent decline.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:01.894
It is true,

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:02.228
Sheriff,

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:03.096
of course, at the jail

00:06:03.096 --> 00:06:04.330
is the focus of a civil rights

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.032
probe by the Justice Department.

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:07.166
Ten inmates have died there

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:07.900
so far this year.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:08.468
The latest death,

00:06:08.468 --> 00:06:10.503
I understand, was earlier this week.

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:12.205
I wanted to give you a chance to respond

00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:13.072
to all of this.

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:16.109
Well, first, let me let me say that

00:06:16.109 --> 00:06:17.477
that's why I was present.

00:06:17.477 --> 00:06:19.045
I wanted to make sure

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:21.848
that when these fake accusations came out

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:22.782
about the facility

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:23.883
and the portion that he was

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:25.752
in, I actually was there.

00:06:25.752 --> 00:06:27.186
And witnessed the portions

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:28.755
that he actually walked

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:30.189
through very briskly.

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:32.792
So to that end, that, again, much like

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:33.793
everything is

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:35.895
is fake news from that perspective,

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:39.799
And then secondly, in terms of the DOJ

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:41.968
and the Justice Department,

00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:43.436
if you go back

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:44.370
and you look at the steps

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:45.138
that we've taken

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:48.808
since I took office and 11611 21,

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:52.111
the focus has been the focus has been

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:53.446
on us, making sure

00:06:53.446 --> 00:06:55.281
we've been very transparent,

00:06:55.281 --> 00:06:56.916
but also let's face it,

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:59.252
I reached out to the Bureau of Justice,

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:00.286
National Institute

00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:00.820
of Corrections

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:02.889
in November of last year

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:04.090
and asked for help.

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.725
We work with our board of Commissioners

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:07.293
to really focus on

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:08.728
how do we create better

00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:10.229
a better environment.

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:11.631
We inherited this.

00:07:11.631 --> 00:07:13.699
There's no mistake about that.

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:15.902
Overcrowding across the country has

00:07:16.402 --> 00:07:17.670
really taken precedence

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:20.139
when you look at the number of arrests,

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:20.973
the number of things

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:23.309
that violent arrests in our facility.

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:25.511
So it seems like an anomaly.

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:26.879
The fact that the jail

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:28.815
is a microcosm of our community

00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:31.050
as a whole really speaks volumes.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.118
But we are focused

00:07:32.118 --> 00:07:33.119
and laser

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:34.520
focused on making sure

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.522
we ask for everything we need

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:38.791
and then get our women and men

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.193
filling out a sheriff's office,

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:42.795
the tools they need to really combat this

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:45.031
this urgent crisis that we have.

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:46.499
And so even earlier today,

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:48.668
I met with the chairman of Fulton

00:07:48.668 --> 00:07:50.269
County Board of Commissioners

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:51.904
so that we could talk about that.

00:07:51.904 --> 00:07:52.171
All right.

00:07:52.171 --> 00:07:53.606
Well, Sheriff, I appreciate your time.

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:55.007
Thank you so much for coming on

00:07:56.242 --> 00:07:56.943
I appreciate it.

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:57.410
Thank you.

